/T (Fifty-nine percent of households have at least one insecticide-treated net \(ITN\). On average, there are 1.3 ITNs per household. Nearly one third \(32%\) of households own at least one ITN for every two people who stayed in the household the night before the survey. Eight in ten households obtained their ITNs from mass distribution campaigns. The state with the lowest ITN ownership rate is Edo at 21%, while the highest is Zamfara, where 90% of households have at least one ITN.)
